  "description": "meme-id: my_face_when_im_wating_for_my_cookies_to_be_done_baking; hasOverallIntent: Harmless Humor; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a solemn religious ceremony, likely a Catholic Mass, with clergy in vestments and ornate church decor. The text overlays humorously juxtapose the serious, reverent atmosphere with the mundane, impatient waiting for cookies to bake. The intent is purely comedic, using the contrast between the sacred setting and the trivial, relatable human experience of waiting for food. There is no toxicity, hate, abuse, or harmful content present. The meme relies on absurdity and relatability, not on targeting any group or promoting harm. The humor stems from the incongruity of the scene and the universal experience of impatience while baking.",
